description = "Independent module S3: the Brunerie / Finster-Mimram type theory of globular weak omega-groupoids and omega-categories — globular contexts, decidable pasting-scheme recognition, source/target boundaries, coherence validity, substitution typing, a coherence library, the triangle-order characterization of pasting schemes, and a sound interpretation in finite-group models"
